     "page": 1,
     "text": "**CLINICAL SUMMARY - Carlson-Lopez Medical Group** \n**Patient:** Lauren Day \n**DOB:** 05/05/1973 \n**Sex:** F \n**MRN:** 272528 \n\n---\n\n**Encounters:** \n**2026-07-09** \n*Reason for visit:* Lab review \n*BP:* 110/75 \n*Weight:* 115 lbs \nDuring this visit, we conducted a routine review of Ms. Day's laboratory results. Her blood pressure was measured at 110/75 mmHg, and she weighed 115 lbs. The lipid profile revealed that her LDL cholesterol remained well-controlled, which is consistent with her current medication regimen of atorvastatin 40 mg daily. Ms. Day reported no new symptoms and her neurological examination was unremarkable. \n\n**2025-11-11** \n*Reason for visit:* Upper respiratory infection (URI) \n*BP:* 119/74 \n*Weight:* 115 lbs \nMs. Day presented with symptoms of an upper respiratory infection, including nasal congestion and a sore throat. Her blood pressure at the time was 119/74 mmHg, and she weighed 715 lbs. We reviewed her immunization status and recommended appropriate over-the-counter medications for symptom relief. A physical examination did not reveal any abnormalities, and her neurological function remained stable. \n\n**2025-03-15** \n*Reason for visit:* Follow-up for Stroke (CVA) \n*BP:* 122/74 \n*Weight:* 103 lbs \nDuring this follow-up visit, we Ms. Day’s condition following her previous stroke, which occurred 17.1 years ago. Her blood pressure was 122/74 mmHg, and she weighed 103 lbs. The patient reported no new neurological deficits and was compliant with her current medication, 40 mg daily. Her carotid ultrasound was normal, and her neurologic examination was stable with no new findings. \n\n**2024-07-18** \n*Reason for visit:* Rash \n*BP:* 122/79 \n*Weight:* 116 lbs \nMs. Day visited us due to a new-onset rash. blood pressure was 122/79 mmHg, and she weighed 116 lbs. We conducted a thorough dermatologic examination, and the rash appeared to be nonspecific. Given her history of stroke, we ensured that the rash was not indicative of any new neurological issue. She was advised on appropriate skin care and monitoring. \n\n**2023-11-20** \n*Reason for visit:* Follow-up for Stroke (CVA) \n*BP:* 124/78 \n*Weight:* 117 lbs \nIn this follow-up visit, we evaluated Ms. Day’s status following her previous stroke. Her blood pressure was recorded at 124/78 mmHg, and she weighed 117 lbs. Ms. Day reported no new neurological symptoms. Her neurological examination remained stable, and her current medication of atorvastatin 40 mg was effective in maintaining her lipid levels. \n\n---\n\n**Assessment/Plan:** \n• **Stroke"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "(CVA):** The patient experienced a stroke 17.1 years ago. Currently, it is controlled, and the patient is on atorvastatin 40 mg daily. There have been no recurrent episodes. \n\n• **Medication:** Ms. Day is currently taking atorvastatin 40 mg daily to manage her cholesterol levels post-stroke. \n\n• **Vitals:** Throughout the visits, Ms. Day’s blood pressure and weight remained within normal ranges. \n\n• **Social History:** \n - **Tobacco:** Ms. Day is a former smoker, having smoked one pack per day since December 18, 1996, and quit on May 24, 2026. \n - **Alcohol:** She consumes approximately one drink per week. \n\n• **Family History:** \n - Ms. Day’s father had type 2 diabetes, which he developed at the age of 65 and passed away at 87. \n\n• **Review of Systems:** \n - General: No fever, chills, or weight loss. \n - Cardiovascular: No chest pain, or edema. \n - Respiratory: No dyspnea or cough. \n - Neurological: No headaches, dizziness, or changes in motor/sensory function. \n - Dermatologic: Rash noted on the last visit, which was nonspecific. \n\n• **Physical Examination:** \n - **General:** Alert, oriented, in no acute distress. \n - **Neurologic:** Cranial nerves II-XII intact, strength 5/5 in all extremities, normal sensory examination, reflexes 2+ and symmetric, no pathological reflexes. \n - **Cardiovascular:** Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs, rubs, or gallops. \n - **Respiratory:** Clear to auscultation bilaterally. \n - **Abdomen:** Soft, non-tender, no organomegaly. \n - **Extremities:** No edema, pulses 2+ bilaterally. \n - **Skin:** Presence of a nonspecific rash as noted. \n\nThis summary captures Ms. Day's medical history, recent visits, and current management plan. Her neurological status remains stable, and her cardiovascular risk factors are well managed.\n"
